+## Simulated printer (testing only)
+
+`run --simulated-printer` tests the order-to-print path with no printer at all. The agent takes
+jobs and follows the usual rules: the server's approval and payment checks, the lease, the
+"printing" record before anything is sent, and the duplicate-print safeguards. The only
+difference is the adapter. It checks that the file is a PDF, keeps a record in memory and reports
+the job as sent. It never runs CUPS, PowerShell, SumatraPDF or any printer command, and its
+messages say **SIMULATED** and "no paper came out".
+
+- Only `run` has this mode. `printers`, `doctor`, `set-printer` and `test-print` always use the
+  real printing system.
+- It starts only when the server address is `localhost` or `127.0.0.1`. Any other address,
+  including the live server, is refused before any request is made.
+- Its results are written to that test server's database as `sent`, the same as a real job. Use a
+  test database only.
+- The simulated printer takes the name of the fallback printer set on this computer, if there is
+  one. Its log lines still say SIMULATED.
+
+```
+qrquick-print-agent run --simulated-printer
+```
+
